dcomp: keep copying a same-process window swap chain when the window composites with alpha

CapCut 9.7 on lab runtime 11.10-183rc: opening the settings-gear menu drew the menu, but the whole rest
of the screen turned dark gray (#202020) and hid CapCut's main window until the menu closed (the old
"black screen with a menu open" bug, now gray). 182 shows the main window around the menu.

Mechanism: every CapCut menu is a screen-sized Qt translucent popup (WS_POPUP, WS_EX_LAYERED|
WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW, LWA_ALPHA 255, DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow, its own CreateSwapChainForHwnd chain,
DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_DISCARD, 1 buffer), transparent except for the menu. Patch 117 + dxvk 0006 made such a
window composite with its pixels' alpha: dwmapi marks it __wine_dwm_alpha, winewayland gives its window
surface the pixels' alpha, DXVK presents its chain PRE_MULTIPLIED. dcomp-hwnd-chain-direct (183rc) stopped
the bridge's copy of a same-process window chain into the window's GDI surface on the premise that DXVK's
Vulkan subsurface hides that surface. For a marked window it does not: the subsurface is see-through
wherever the frame is, and the GDI surface underneath still held the popup's unreplaced #202020 fill
(GDI pixels stay opaque), which until 183rc the copy overwrote with the frame (alpha 0 around the menu).
With NEUTRON_DXVK_PREMULTIPLIED=0 the same area is black instead of gray: the gray is under the subsurface.

Windows: a bitblt-model Present (DISCARD / SEQUENTIAL) copies the back buffer into the window's DWM
redirection surface, the surface GDI also draws to ("DXGI flip model", Microsoft Learn: "In the bitblt
model, contents of the back buffer are copied into the redirection surface on each call to Present1"),
and with blur-behind DWM blends that surface by its alpha channel ("DWM Blur Behind Overview"). Nothing
of the earlier GDI fill survives under the frame. The bridge's copy is Wine's version of that copy, so a
window carrying __wine_dwm_alpha (the same mark DXVK reads to choose PRE_MULTIPLIED) keeps it. Windows
without the mark keep the direct path and its savings. One log line per window that keeps the copy
("neutron-hwnd-direct: ... still copied").

The mark is read at every Present (one GetPropW for same-process window chains only; Topaz and Live
numbers below include it). Not covered: a fully transparent frame (all pixels 0) is still skipped by the
bridge's uniform-black guard and leaves the GDI fill showing (as in 182). The frame's alpha is applied twice where the copy and the subsurface overlap
(menu shadow), as in 182 (menu box incl. shadow pixel-identical to 182, max difference 1). Flip-model
blur-behind windows also keep the copy (none seen; Windows shows only the frame there, which the copy
approximates better than the bare GDI surface).

Lab (desk v, hand-paced: wait for the Pro promo, close it with its X, wait, click the gear; menu open
verified in every capture): 183rc gray 2/2, 182 main window visible 2/2 (fresh copies); on 183rc only
NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY=1 brings the main window back (2/2; FLIP_DISCARD_BUF0=0, OWNER_TOPMOST=0,
OWNED_RECONF_KEEPZ=0 stay gray 2/2 each). Lab runtime 11.10-183v (183rc + this dcomp): main window visible
2/2 on fresh copies, 3 windows per run keep the copy (main, promo, menu; effect 0, 1 buffer); kill switch
NEUTRON_DCOMP_DWM_ALPHA_COPY=0 on the same build: gray 2/2. The savings stay: Topaz Photo sign-in screen
53.7% / 53.6% of a core, 0 copies (main window not marked) vs 76.2% with NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY=1;
Ableton Live 12 Welcome 12.8% / 12.9%, 0 copies vs 56.4%. CapCut itself copies only changed frames (91 in a run).

Applies after dcomp-flip-discard-buffer0 and dcomp-hwnd-chain-direct (same file). Kill switch
NEUTRON_DCOMP_DWM_ALPHA_COPY=0.

--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c	2026-11-05 20:25:32.147562657 -0500
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c	2026-11-05 22:44:04.398987105 -0500
@@ -403,6 +403,30 @@
     return 0;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON 2026-11-05 (capcut183): the direct path below is right only while DXVK's Vulkan subsurface hides
+ * the window's GDI surface, i.e. while DXVK presents it OPAQUE. A window that called
+ * DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow carries the __wine_dwm_alpha mark (dwmapi); DXVK then composites its present
+ * PRE_MULTIPLIED and winewayland gives the window surface its pixels' alpha, so the GDI surface shows
+ * wherever the frame is not opaque. On Windows nothing is underneath: a bitblt-model Present copies the
+ * frame into the window's redirection surface, the very surface GDI draws to, and DWM blends that by its
+ * alpha (docs: "DXGI flip model", bitblt vs flip). The bridge's copy is Wine's version of that copy, so
+ * it stays for marked windows. CapCut 9.7: every menu is a screen-sized Qt translucent popup
+ * (WS_EX_LAYERED|WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW, blur-behind, its own swap chain); without the copy the area around the
+ * menu showed the popup's unreplaced GDI fill (#202020) over the whole work area.
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_DCOMP_DWM_ALPHA_COPY=0 (skip the copy for marked windows too, as 183rc did). */
+static BOOL neutron_dwm_alpha_copy(HWND hwnd)
+{
+    static int gate = -1;
+
+    if (gate < 0)
+    {
+        char b[8];
+        gate = (GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_DCOMP_DWM_ALPHA_COPY", b, sizeof(b)) && b[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1;
+        ERR("neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_DCOMP_DWM_ALPHA_COPY = %d\n", gate);
+    }
+    return gate && GetPropW(hwnd, L"__wine_dwm_alpha");
+}
+
 /* NEUTRON 2026-11-05: a swap chain created for a window (CreateSwapChainForHwnd) reaches the screen through
  * that window on Windows -- DWM composes it, nothing copies it anywhere else. DXVK presents it into the
  * window's own Vulkan client surface, which winewayland shows above the window's GDI surface (unless
@@ -426,7 +450,23 @@
     }
     if (copy || suppress || !hwnd) return FALSE;
     if (FAILED(IDXGISwapChain_GetDesc(swapchain, &scd))) return FALSE;
-    return scd.OutputWindow == hwnd && scd.Windowed;
+    if (scd.OutputWindow != hwnd || !scd.Windowed) return FALSE;
+    if (neutron_dwm_alpha_copy(hwnd))
+    {
+        static HWND logged[16]; /* one line per window (this runs on every Present) */
+        static unsigned int nlogged;
+        unsigned int i;
+
+        for (i = 0; i < nlogged; i++) if (logged[i] == hwnd) break;
+        if (i == nlogged && nlogged < ARRAY_SIZE(logged))
+        {
+            logged[nlogged++] = hwnd;
+            ERR("neutron-hwnd-direct: hwnd=%p effect=%u buffers=%u blur-behind -> still copied (its window "
+                "surface shows through DXVK's pre-multiplied present)\n", hwnd, scd.SwapEffect, scd.BufferCount);
+        }
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+    return TRUE;
 }
 
 /* NEUTRON bounded-acquire handshake (round 32). Private DXVK interface --
